A small group survived on Wrangel Island, off the coast of Siberia, until about 4,000 years ago. [[@sea-level-rise|Rising seas]] had cut the island off, and no people lived there yet. By then, the [[@pyramids|Great Pyramid]] of Egypt had already been standing for about 500 years.

The island group was small, and studies of their DNA suggest they had become inbred, with many faults in their [[gene|genes]]. Nobody knows exactly what finished them. It might have been a bad winter, a [[drought|drought]] or a disease.

{{story:pyramids}}

भारत में जंगल की ज़्यादातर आगें लगभग फ़रवरी से जून के बीच, मानसून से पहले, लगती हैं, जब पत्ते झड़ चुके होते हैं और ज़मीन सूखी होती है। भारतीय वन सर्वेक्षण [[@satellites-help|उपग्रहों]] से आग पर नज़र रखता है और वन अधिकारियों को चेतावनियाँ भेजता है।

[[@uttarakhand|उत्तराखंड]] की पहाड़ियों में अक्सर आग के बुरे मौसम आते हैं। वहाँ के चीड़ के जंगल पत्तियों की मोटी चादर गिराते हैं, जो आसानी से जलती है। भारत में जंगल की बहुत-सी आगें जान-बूझकर लगाई जाती हैं, ज़मीन साफ़ करने, मवेशियों के लिए ताज़ी घास उगाने या वन-उपज इकट्ठा करने के लिए, और इनमें से कुछ बेक़ाबू हो जाती हैं। ओडिशा, मध्य प्रदेश और छत्तीसगढ़ जैसे मध्य भारत के राज्यों में भी हर साल बहुत आगें दर्ज होती हैं।

{{story:fire-burns}}

Male mosquitoes never bite. Both males and females drink nectar from flowers for energy. As they do, some carry [[pollen|pollen]] from one flower to another.

A few plants, such as certain orchids in North America's northern forests, are pollinated mainly by mosquitoes. Losing mosquitoes might hurt them, though other insects could help.

{{story:mosquito-diseases}}

The International [[@space-station|Space Station]] orbits about 400 km up, roughly as far as Mumbai is from Goa. It goes around Earth roughly every 90 minutes, so the crew sees about 16 sunrises and sunsets every day.

Astronauts on board still feel about 90% of the gravity we feel on the ground. They float because the station and everything inside it are falling together. If you were in a lift whose cable snapped, you would float inside it for a moment too, for the same reason.

{{story:gravity-fall}}

Earth is curved, so a light at sea level disappears below the horizon quite quickly. The higher the light, the farther it can be seen. A lamp 50 m above the sea can be seen from a ship's deck roughly 30 km away, well before the ship reaches danger.

That is why lighthouses are tall, or are built on top of cliffs. The famous Pharos of Alexandria in Egypt, built more than 2,000 years ago, may have been around 100 m tall. It was one of the [[@seven-wonders|Seven Wonders]] of the ancient world and stood for many centuries before earthquakes brought it down.

{{story:lenses-glasses}}

The [[@blue-whale|blue whale]] can grow to about 30 metres long, a little longer than a basketball court, or about one and a half Mumbai local train coaches. It eats tiny shrimp-like animals called krill and small fish, gulping huge mouthfuls of water and pushing it out through brush-like plates.

In 2015, people in boats off Sindhudurg in Maharashtra filmed blue whales close to the coast, which surprised many. Whale watchers often see them near Mirissa and Trincomalee in Sri Lanka, not far from India's southern tip. Scientists think some of these whales may live in the northern Indian Ocean all year, instead of travelling to Antarctica.

{{story:whales-walked}}

The Lake Pontchartrain Causeway is two side-by-side bridges across a lake near New Orleans. In the middle, drivers can travel for several kilometres and see no land at all, only water and the road ahead.

China's Hong Kong–Zhuhai–Macau link, opened in 2018, runs about 55 kilometres across the sea. Part of it dives into an undersea tunnel between two artificial islands, so that big ships can sail over the top.

{{story:puzzle-konigsberg}}

The oldest known mirrors are about 8,000 years old. They were made from obsidian, a black volcanic glass, polished until it shone, and were found at Çatalhöyük in present-day Turkey. Later, people in Egypt, the Indus Valley, China and Mesoamerica polished bronze, copper and other stones.

In 1835, the German chemist Justus von Liebig found a way to coat glass with a thin, even layer of real silver using chemicals. Mirrors soon became cheap enough for ordinary homes.

{{story:apollo-moon}}

In most cultures, children take their father's [[@names-world|family name]]. But some societies trace family through the mother, called matrilineal descent. The Khasi and Garo peoples of [[@meghalaya|Meghalaya]] in [[@northeast-india|northeast India]] are well-known examples. Among the Khasi, children belong to their mother's clan, and the youngest daughter traditionally [[inherit|inherits]] the family home and cares for her parents.

In [[@kerala|Kerala]], many Nair families once lived in large matrilineal households called *tharavads*. That system faded in the 20th century, after new laws changed how property was inherited.

{{story:names-meaning}}

Dharavi, in Mumbai, is one of Asia's best-known slums. It covers a little over 2 square kilometres, about as much land as 300 football fields, and estimates of its population range from a few lakh to around 10 lakh.

Dharavi is also a place of work. Potters fire pots in Kumbharwada. Leather goods, clothes, snacks and soap are made in small rooms. Thousands of people sort and clean plastic and metal for [[@recycling|recycling]], turning the city's waste into raw material again. Many homes are also workplaces, with a sewing machine by the bed or a [[kiln|kiln]] in the lane. Goods made here are sold across India and sometimes abroad.

{{story:recycling}}

In farming villages, the year follows the crops and the rain. Fields are ploughed and sown when the [[@monsoon|monsoon]] arrives in June or July. Paddy, cotton, maize or millets grow through the wet months and are harvested in autumn. In many places, a second crop such as wheat or mustard is grown through winter.

A good [[monsoon|monsoon]] can mean a good year. A weak one can mean debt and worry, especially for farmers without wells or canals. That is why many [[@festivals-unity|village festivals]], from Pongal in Tamil Nadu to Baisakhi in Punjab, are harvest celebrations.

{{story:monsoon}}

The dust storms came again and again. On 14 April 1935, now called Black Sunday, a massive storm swept across Oklahoma and Texas. Witnesses said the sky turned black in minutes, birds fled ahead of it and people crawled home along fences. It is thought to have carried hundreds of thousands of tonnes of soil.

Dust got everywhere. It piled up against houses like snow drifts and buried fences and tractors. Families hung wet sheets over windows and still woke up with dust on their pillows. Many children and older people fell ill with "dust pneumonia", a lung illness caused by breathing in the fine soil.

{{story:great-depression}}

During the French Revolution, scientists in Paris helped create the metre and the kilogram, so that everyone could measure the same way. The [[@metric-system|metric system]] is now used by almost every country.

{{story:metric-system}}

In 2024, Paris hosted the [[@olympics|Olympics]] for the third time, with the opening ceremony held on boats along the Seine instead of in a stadium. Athletes sailed past the Louvre and Notre-Dame, and the Olympic cauldron rose into the sky beneath a giant balloon.

मूँगफली की खेती सबसे पहले दक्षिण अमेरिका में हुई, शायद आज के बोलीविया और उत्तरी अर्जेंटीना के आसपास, हज़ारों साल पहले। 1500 के दशक में स्पेनी और पुर्तगाली नाविक इसे अफ़्रीका, एशिया और यूरोप ले गए।

भारत ने इसे झट से अपना लिया। आज चीन के बाद भारत दुनिया में मूँगफली का दूसरा सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है, और सबसे ज़्यादा मूँगफली गुजरात उगाता है। मूँगफली [[@indian-breakfasts|पोहे]], चिक्की, चटनी, साबूदाना खिचड़ी और [[@oils-cooking|मूँगफली के तेल]] में जाती है। और काग़ज़ के कोन में भुनी मूँगफली तो हर समुद्र-तट और रेलवे स्टेशन पर बिकती है।

